course: dictionary
lesson: 14916
title: Redrafting your writing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Writers rarely get it right the first time. A first go at a story is called a draft. When you write it again to make it better, that is a redraft. You might fix spelling, choose better words, change the order of sentences or improve the ending.
explain: Look at this first try: «My dog is big. He runs fast.» Now the redraft: «My huge dog sprints across the field.» The story is the same, but the writing is stronger. To redraft means to write again, making it better.
explain: Redrafting is one step in writing: plan, draft, edit, redraft, publish. Each step helps the next one. If your first draft needs changes, that is normal. Redrafting is how a piece of writing gets better.
fact: Redraft is a verb and a noun: you can redraft a story, or write a new redraft.
fact: To redraft means to write a piece of writing again, making it better.
fact: A redraft is a new, improved version of a piece of writing.
fact: Redrafting can mean fixing spelling, adding better words, changing the order or improving the ending.
fact: In adult life, laws, letters and plans are redrafted too.
exercise: «Please redraft your story before you publish it.» What does redraft mean here? | Count the words | Read it out loud to the class | *Write it again, making it better | Throw it away and never write again
exercise: What is a redraft? | *A new, improved version of a piece of writing | A pen used for writing | A type of spelling test | A picture drawn in the margin
exercise: In the writing steps plan, draft, edit, redraft, publish, which step comes after edit? | Draft | Publish | Plan | *Redraft
test: Which phrase best shows redrafting? | Reading your story once | Copying your first draft exactly | *Rewriting your story to add better words | Tearing up your story and leaving it
test: «I will redraft my letter.» What will the writer do? | *Write the letter again to make it better | Post the letter without changes | Lose the letter | Read the letter to the dog
exam: Which word is the past tense of redraft? | *Redrafted | Redrafting | A redraft | Redrafts
